PREDECLARED CAPABILITY MAPPING
  state read             -> View
  live event stream      -> View
  new subscription       -> View
  indirect actuation     -> Operate
  direct actuation       -> Operate
  script execution       -> Manage
  event firing           -> Manage
  user enumeration       -> Administer

HIGHEST SURVIVING CAPABILITY PER TRANSITION
  arm                     n  highest surviving   surviving operations
  user/delete            30  View                state read, live event stream
  user/deactivate        30  none                (none)
  admin/delete           30  Administer          state read, live event stream, new subscription, indirect actuation, event firing, user enumeration
  admin/deactivate       30  none                (none)

READING
  An ordinary member's removal leaves View. An administrator's removal leaves
  Administer - the top of the lattice - because user enumeration survives, and
  it leaves Operate through the composed deputy path while DIRECT actuation is
  denied. Severity therefore scales with the role held at the moment of removal,
  and the highest surviving capability separates the two arms that a binary
  residue flag would report identically.
